#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054611 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67b307f2-1d37-5741-8972-cbddae50c4c8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Product of Two Functions"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98638830-1bd5-5922-b12a-9c190db0e3da" :question/math-academy-id "q-4825" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+5x$ and $g(x)=9-2x,$ find $(fg)(-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $(fg)(x)$ means  the product of the functions  $f(x)$ and $g(x).$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo evaluate $(fg)(-1),$ we find $f(-1)$ and $g(-1),$ and then multiply the results.\n\nFirst, we find $f(-1)$ and $g(-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =2(-1)^{2}+5(-1)=-3 \\\\ g(-1) & =9-2(-1)=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply the results:\n\n$$\n(fg)(-1)=f(-1)g(-1)=-3\\cdot 11=-33\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we find $(fg)(x)$ by multiplying the two functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(fg)(x) & =(2{x}^{2}+5x)(9-2x) \\\\  & =-4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+45x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate $(fg)(-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(fg)(-1) & =-4(-1)^{3}+8(-1)^{2}+45(-1) \\\\  & =4+8-45 \\\\  & =-33\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054612 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55d291ea-d722-5852-9c3a-faaba8e6df3e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Quotient of Two Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a971ff-a0ac-5e41-a6f9-de3fae7b9090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413834} {:answer/id #uuid "79f9695d-1add-50ce-be55-ea88b6f4de22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413843} {:answer/id #uuid "970de561-023f-5e4a-8ecd-0cd2dba960b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413846} {:answer/id #uuid "e137be1f-e344-5693-8401-73a72931c8a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413852} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2ca1be-c620-54b9-9e8c-878f37709564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "970de561-023f-5e4a-8ecd-0cd2dba960b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413846} :answer-field/id #uuid "328f71c0-868a-51e6-9077-92f3e52307b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d54abce-95cd-5dd9-be80-9f173369bea7" :question/math-academy-id "q-66425" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-6$ and $g(x)=-2x+2,$ find  $(f/g)(3).$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $(f/g)(x)$ means the quotient of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x).$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo evaluate $(f/g)(3),$ we find $f(3)$ and $g(3),$ and then divide the results.\n\nFirst, we find $f(3)$ and $g(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =2(3)^{2}-6=12 \\\\ g(3) & =-2(3)+2=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we divide the results:\n\n$$\n(f/g)(3)=\\frac{f(3)}{g(3)}=\\frac{12}{-4}=-3\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we find $(f/g)(x)$ by dividing $f$ by $g$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f/g)(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}-6}{-2x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate $(f/g)(3):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f/g)(3) & =\\frac{2(3)^{2}-6}{-2(3)+2}=\\frac{12}{-4}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
